    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0117" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/148<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >3/12</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-20T10:00:00-05:00">June 20, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 57, June 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d126-f1"/> a conference was held between the Ministers of Foreign
                    Affairs and National Defense, Canaga, Harris and myself with regard to the
                    defense of the Americas, last night. The Foreign Minister reasserted Ecuador’s
                    intention to stand by conference agreements and both Tobar and Plaza asserted
                    the disposition of their Government to cooperate in every practical way. They
                    are also prepared to hold staff conferences any time after July 10.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
